ledge with upper wdata bits set being honoured; (9) rising-edge mode, where a held level does not pend again and a falling edge does not pend; (10) mixed edge and level modes. A 400-cycle pseudo-random phase (xorshift, fixed seed) follows. Its stimulus is sparse sources, random register writes and acknowledges aimed at the current claim, all checked against the model. INTENT: every RTL line and both arms of every if, case and ternary should execute, including the out-of-range acknowledge and the default (CLAIM) case arm. UNREACHABLE TOGGLE POINTS at N = 8 cannot be closed by any stimulus. (a) rdata[30:8] is always 0: register reads drive only bits N-1:0, and the CLAIM read drives only bits 31 and 4:0. (b) irq_id[4:3] is always 0, because the highest source number is 7. (c) unused_wdata is the constant &{1'b0, wdata} = 0, which the tool may also optimise away. These gaps are justified by the RTL text above, not hidden: the testbench uses no coverage pragma, include, Verilator configuration, $fopen, $system, $c or DPI. Closing them needs a run with N = 32 (the model is parametric, but the directed expected values assume N = 8) or a waiver signed off by the designer. The line, toggle and branch percentages from the platform's coverage.read run on this testbench are not yet available, and the coverage bounds were not provided to this seat."}], "files": [{"path": "irq_ctrl_cov_tb.sv", "kind": "testbench", "title": "irq_ctrl_cov_tb.sv: self-checking coverage testbench for irq_ctrl (N=8)", "summary": "Extends the approved idle testbench [artifact:prj-63d6b8e26c.testbench.a1] for the approved RTL [artifact:prj-63d6b8e26c.design-under-test.a1] under requirement [requirement:req-1e26d9c190]. It adds a per-cycle reference-model scoreboard, directed scenarios (reset, register access, W1C, level and edge detection, detection-wins-over-clear, priority, masking, out-of-range acknowledge, mixed modes, mid-run reset) and a 400-cycle seeded random phase. It ends with the same NIRMAAN